The '''Scarred Womb''' is one of the environments in [[Chapter 4]] added in ''[[Afterbirth]]''. The theme of the Scarred Womb is wounded and scarred tissue, grafted skin, and early stages of decay. The floor looks much like a failed surgery, with stapled skin being plastered onto the womb's walls being this floor's alt. backdrop. Most new enemies featured in The Scarred Womb are damaged and grievously injured variations of other enemies, such as Fistuloids and Lepers. {{dlc|nr}} Rocks have a chance to be replaced with {{E|Red Poop}}.

The Scarred Womb's alternate floors are the {{s|Womb}} and the {{s|Utero}}. Similarly to these, from this floor onward, {{r|Treasure Room}}s and {{r|Shop}}s will no longer naturally generate and all damage that is taken deducts a full heart from Isaac's HP (unless he has {{i|The Wafer}}), regardless of the source.

{{dlc|a+}} The Scarred Womb is unlocked by defeating {{e|It Lives!}} 30 times. Killing {{e|Dogma}} and {{e|The Beast}} also increases this tally, as does {{s|Mausoleum}}'s version of Mom's Heart.

