== Trivia ==
* Before the proper release of ''Afterbirth'', the Scarred Womb was to be named "Rotten Womb".
* The stitches on the walls and floor faintly resemble the {{e|Fistula}} boss.
* Using {{i|Flush!}} on the scarred womb will flood the room with red liquid (likely blood) instead of water.
* {{dlc|a+}} Previously, {{e|Mom's Heart}} could appear in the Scarred Womb. However, as of [[Booster Packs#Booster Pack #5|Booster Pack #5]], since it is required to defeat It Lives! 30 times to unlock the Scarred Womb, Mom's Heart can no longer appear in it.
{{clear}}

== Music ==
* The [[music]] for the Scarred Womb is titled ''Cicatrix''.<ref>[https://ridiculon.bandcamp.com/album/the-binding-of-isaac-afterbirth-ost Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth OST]</ref>
* A cicatrix is a medical term for a scar, as well as the Latin term for "scar".
* The music heard during the fight against Mom's Heart/It Lives! is called ''Ventricide''. Ventricide combines ventricle, a word that means a hollow area in an organ and is often associated with the heart, and the suffix -cide, which denotes the act of killing.

